<title>USA: Freddie Mac to redeem $300 mln in debentures.</title>
<headline>Freddie Mac to redeem $300 mln in debentures.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freddie Mac said Thursday that on June 2 it will redeem fixed-rate debenture issues totaling $300 in their entirety as follows.</p>
<p>    Principal Interest	Maturity	 Cusip</p>
<p>     $200 million   7.88	  4/28/04	313400G98</p>
<p>     $100 million   7.89	  5/12/04	313400J79</p>
<p>The debentures will be redeemed at a price equal to 100 percent of the principal amount.</p>
<p>Payment of principal plus interest accrued to the redemption date will be made to shareholders of record as of the close of business on May 30, 1997, Freddie Mac said.</p>
<p>Freddie Mac is a corporation chartered by Congress that buys mortgages from lenders and packages them into securities for investors.</p>
</text>
